{
 "id": "bigville_fisc_state",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "depends_on": [],
 "self_load_only": true,
 "description": "BIGVILLE R9 (block 257000) -- the STATE / FISCAL institution: taxes on landowners+workers at a rate SET BY THE COUNCIL (fs_set_tax: a decision_value = base_rate_bp + capture_premium_bp, the TWIN of R7's bank rate -- a FAIR council premium=0, a CAPTURED John's council premium>0) -> a `Treasury` purse (fs_collect: tax_due = IDiv(taxable*rate+5000, 10000), INTEGER coin, the cross-frame rate applied INTENSIONALLY) -> the MAYOR's salary + the CONSTABLE's wage (fs_pay_salary, funded iff the purse can afford it; fs_salary_unfunded marks the public service FAILED when it can't). fs_treasury_empty flags a depleted purse (public works fail). fs_graft is MAYORAL CORRUPTION gated on corrupt=1 (the failing control: a fair mayor never matches -> the purse sustains; a corrupt one drains it to his PERSONAL coin -- the principal/agent divergence, the state twin of the greedy banker). fs_levy is the POOLING force (coin flows workers->the wealthy -- the R7 interest-attractor essence, honestly stand-in) that the tax+salary REDISTRIBUTION loop BREAKS. Composes existing Terms; zero new Rust; self_load_only so it cannot affect any other suite.",
